# The drives as the BIOS describes them, in the boot information (roadmap
# disk-scheduler.md M2, D16): the loader asks INT 13h AH=15h for each
# diskette drive's type (1: 360 KB, no change line; 2: 1.2 MB, a change
# line), and copies each fixed disk's parameter table, which INT 41h and 46h
# point to, when CMOS 12h gives the disk a type. Bochs's BIOS gives both
# disks their geometry; its precompensation is "none" (FFFFh) and its
# control byte 8 (more than 8 heads: 0, its default). MAME's CMOS says no
# fixed disk (docs/emulators.md), so its drivers take disks.inc's.
program: idle
define: TEST_GEOMETRY
match: contains
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs
---
root: diskette drives' types: {...} {...}
root: fixed disk 0: 615 cylinders, 4 heads, 17 sectors, precompensation from {...}
root: fixed disk 1: 306 cylinders, 4 heads, 17 sectors, precompensation from {...}
